Review these previously model-flagged conflict pairs against the supplied quotations and scope/date fields. Do not assume every pair is a conflict. Different products, origins, tariff programs, or dated stages are not automatically contradictory. Only use apparent_same_scope_conflict when the supplied claims appear incompatible on the same scope/date; otherwise distinguish dated progression, differing scope, complementary claims, and missing scope. Do not verify current law from memory. Explain the reason briefly for every pair.
UNTRUSTED_EVIDENCE_JSON:
{"research_date": "2026-09-10", "pairs": [{"pair_id": "conflict_f17eee23a7a4805fe5f244cb", "claim_ids": ["claim_081e9d81465ab1c7ae52b523", "claim_5ba21cb6b8d31faaed857335"], "query_ids": ["q_336"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_081e9d81465ab1c7ae52b523", "quote": "The remaining 10-20% are imported, primarily from Mexico, where products that meet USMCA (United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement) origin requirements are not subject to tariffs.", "url": "https://www.idtechex.com/en/research-article/us-tariffs-impact-on-the-ev-charging-market/33089", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"exporting_country": "Mexico"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_5ba21cb6b8d31faaed857335", "quote": "With 80% of US transformers imported, primarily from Mexico and China, tariffs and long lead times exacerbate supply chain bottlenecks.", "url": "https://theevreport.com/us-tariffs-impact-ev-charging-market", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"exporting_country": "Mexico and China"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_15f53959778c000084fa2f31", "claim_ids": ["claim_5f4b9a7a68ef7d2416145f3e", "claim_cc36d53b271a66fc6b2a135e"], "query_ids": ["q_336"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_5f4b9a7a68ef7d2416145f3e", "quote": "Yura Co. Ltd. 854 Sicheong-ro, Paltan-myeon Hwaseong-si, Gyeonggi-do 18529 South Korea", "url": "https://www.customsmobile.com/rulings/docview?doc_id=NY+N359115&highlight=category%3ATrade+Agreement", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Yura Co. Ltd."}}, {"claim_id": "claim_cc36d53b271a66fc6b2a135e", "quote": "The merchandise under consideration is a Liquid-Cooled High-Power EV Charging Cable Assembly, part number S8600-YR05X-A0-USG.", "url": "https://www.customsmobile.com/rulings/docview?doc_id=NY+N359115&highlight=category%3ATrade+Agreement", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"affected_product": "S8600-YR05X-A0-USG"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_457ea564d2af697fd64479c1", "claim_ids": ["claim_cf2f9330f9c127c17df9ff19", "claim_d26b755941ddbd5bbb4526e4"], "query_ids": ["q_336"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_cf2f9330f9c127c17df9ff19", "quote": "The applicable subheading for the Liquid-Cooled High-Power EV Charging Cable Assembly, part number S8600-YR05X-A0-USG will be 8544.42.9090, Harmonized Tariff Schedule of the United States (HTSUS)", "url": "https://www.customsmobile.com/rulings/docview?doc_id=NY+N359115&highlight=category%3ATrade+Agreement", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"hts_code": "8544.42.9090", "chapter_99_code": "Subchapter III to Chapter 99, HTSUS"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_d26b755941ddbd5bbb4526e4", "quote": "The general rate of duty will be 2.6% ad valorem.", "url": "https://www.customsmobile.com/rulings/docview?doc_id=NY+N359115&highlight=category%3ATrade+Agreement", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "2.6%"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_ef11af0074f7bfcc1cc5a7c1", "claim_ids": ["claim_85ca700c12f77e2b2fd87c59", "claim_edb0f7977c30475564d1f191"], "query_ids": ["q_336"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_85ca700c12f77e2b2fd87c59", "quote": "Tariffs on copper and steel may raise costs for EV charger cables and enclosures.", "url": "https://theevreport.com/us-tariffs-impact-ev-charging-market", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Tariffs on copper and steel", "affected_product": "EV charger cables and enclosures"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_edb0f7977c30475564d1f191", "quote": "Additionally, materials such as copper, steel, and aluminum are not subject to new additional reciprocal tariffs (but are subject to 25% Section 232 tariffs).", "url": "https://www.idtechex.com/en/research-article/us-tariffs-impact-on-the-ev-charging-market/33089", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 232 tariffs"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_5181df178b52ac65dc552769", "claim_ids": ["claim_7f7184e447ee0ba1ec32bd36", "claim_9ef4b2390772e771faa2d585"], "query_ids": ["q_336"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_7f7184e447ee0ba1ec32bd36", "quote": "The active 25% tariff on all steel and aluminum imports could raise costs for charger enclosures/housing, mounting systems, and conduit and cable trays.", "url": "https://www.idtechex.com/en/research-article/us-tariffs-impact-on-the-ev-charging-market/33089", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "25%"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_9ef4b2390772e771faa2d585", "quote": "The rate and effective date for tariffs on copper are yet to be determined by the Department of Commerce's investigation.", "url": "https://www.idtechex.com/en/research-article/us-tariffs-impact-on-the-ev-charging-market/33089", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "Department of Commerce", "reported_policy_status": "yet to be determined"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_8fda15c7036c8bd214fcafde", "claim_ids": ["claim_65916cbabc7edeeacee9cdd8", "claim_e7a6f3a0545d1c70493df8ed"], "query_ids": ["q_337"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_65916cbabc7edeeacee9cdd8", "quote": "The tariff rate is set to surge from 25% to 100% starting in 2024.", "url": "https://www.batterytechonline.com/battery-news/new-us-tariffs-designed-to-protect-ev-battery-industries-from-china-trade-practices", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "New US Tariffs Designed to Protect EV/Battery Industries from China Trade Practices", "affected_product": "Electric Vehicles (EVs)", "duty_rate": "100%", "effective_date": "2024"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_e7a6f3a0545d1c70493df8ed", "quote": "Anticipate a hike from 7.5% to 25% by 2024.", "url": "https://www.batterytechonline.com/battery-news/new-us-tariffs-designed-to-protect-ev-battery-industries-from-china-trade-practices", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "New US Tariffs Designed to Protect EV/Battery Industries from China Trade Practices", "affected_product": "Lithium-ion EV Batteries", "duty_rate": "25%", "effective_date": "2024"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_38c73d4586dbd680fadeeb89", "claim_ids": ["claim_302babf871b4fc0d4b64b6d2", "claim_92e2810be6bf8f75786cd380"], "query_ids": ["q_339"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_302babf871b4fc0d4b64b6d2", "quote": "A few weeks ago, President Trump announced a 25% tariff on goods from Mexico and Canada. He followed that announcement by issuing an exemption – expiring April 2 – for autos and auto parts. Another exemption was later issued for imports that comply with the US-Mexico-Canada Agreement on trade (USMCA).", "url": "https://www.asashop.org/2025/04/04/understanding-the-new-tariffs-and-their-potential-impact-on-auto-repairers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "25% tariff"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_92e2810be6bf8f75786cd380", "quote": "On March 26, the Trump Administration announced a 25 percent tariff on imports of automobiles and certain automotive parts. The tariff went into effect for fully assembled vehicles on April 3. The tariff on auto parts will go into effect on May 3.", "url": "https://www.asashop.org/2025/04/04/understanding-the-new-tariffs-and-their-potential-impact-on-auto-repairers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "25 percent tariff", "legal_authority": "Trump Administration", "effective_date": "April 3"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_87b0c284f97d7cd4ee1f7375", "claim_ids": ["claim_a5d1c6eb98f577308e8298fb", "claim_cd08fc85d4da8f651a49107f"], "query_ids": ["q_340"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_a5d1c6eb98f577308e8298fb", "quote": "The tariff on imports from China is currently 145%, but windshields and other automotive items imported from China will just be subject to a 25% tariff.", "url": "https://glassbytes.com/2025/04/expert-breaks-down-tariffs-windshields-are-a-big-one", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"duty_rate": "25%", "effective_date": "currently"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_cd08fc85d4da8f651a49107f", "quote": "China faces a more unique situation. In January, President Trump imposed a 20 percent tariff on all goods from China. That means that a windshield wiper manufactured in China will face a 45 percent import tariff starting on May 3.", "url": "https://www.asashop.org/2025/04/04/understanding-the-new-tariffs-and-their-potential-impact-on-auto-repairers", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"country_of_origin": "China", "duty_rate": "45 percent import tariff", "effective_date": "May 3"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_7a10a296f936a91b6e0ad273", "claim_ids": ["claim_34ac6ca10afd93472961e549", "claim_b25aa366cd165ab527f7b759"], "query_ids": ["q_341"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_34ac6ca10afd93472961e549", "quote": "Commerce will issue antidumping duty orders on imports of these products from Korea, Taiwan, and Thailand, and a countervailing duty order on imports of these products from Vietnam.", "url": "https://www.usitc.gov/keywords/passenger_vehicle_and_light_truck_tires", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "countervailing duty order", "affected_product": "these products"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_b25aa366cd165ab527f7b759", "quote": "Commerce will issue antidumping duty orders on imports of these products from Korea, Taiwan, and Thailand, and a countervailing duty order on imports of these products from Vietnam.", "url": "https://www.usitc.gov/keywords/passenger_vehicle_and_light_truck_tires", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "antidumping duty orders", "affected_product": "these products"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_a8357553daa3f505428975cd", "claim_ids": ["claim_580652bd7994fdbe08cb6413", "claim_6f6e976270eb0641856b108a"], "query_ids": ["q_341"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_580652bd7994fdbe08cb6413", "quote": "As a result of the finding of negligibility, the antidumping duty investigation regarding imports of these products from Vietnam will be terminated.", "url": "https://www.usitc.gov/keywords/passenger_vehicle_and_light_truck_tires", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "antidumping duty investigation", "affected_product": "these products", "reported_policy_status": "terminated"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_6f6e976270eb0641856b108a", "quote": "As a result of the Commission’s affirmative determinations, the U.S. Department of Commerce will continue with its antidumping and countervailing duty investigations concerning imports of these products from Korea, Taiwan, Thailand, and Vietnam", "url": "https://www.usitc.gov/keywords/passenger_vehicle_and_light_truck_tires", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "antidumping and countervailing duty investigations", "affected_product": "these products"}}]}]}
